I can't create files in this session because I only have read and search tools, so here is the server to paste in. The workspace has no existing Node project; it only contains some unrelated Flipper Zero skill files.

**`package.json`**
```json
{
  "name": "time-server",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "main": "server.js",
  "type": "module",
  "scripts": {
    "start": "node server.js"
  },
  "dependencies": {
    "express": "^5.1.0"
  }
}
```

**`server.js`**
```js
import express from "express";

const app = express();
const PORT = process.env.PORT || 3000;

app.get("/time", (req, res) => {
  const now = new Date();
  res.json({
    iso: now.toISOString(),
    unix: Math.floor(now.getTime() / 1000),
    timezone: Intl.DateTimeFormat().resolvedOptions().timeZone,
    local: now.toString(),
  });
});

app.get("/", (req, res) => {
  res.redirect("/time");
});

app.listen(PORT, () => {
  console.log(`Time server listening on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
});
```

**To run it:**
```bash
npm install
npm start
curl http://localhost:3000/time
```

**Example response** (the values will differ):
```json
{
  "iso": "2026-10-16T14:03:12.481Z",
  "unix": 1792159392,
  "timezone": "UTC",
  "local": "Fri Oct 16 2026 14:03:12 GMT+0000 (Coordinated Universal Time)"
}
```

- `GET /time` returns the current time as an ISO 8601 string in UTC, a Unix timestamp in seconds, and the server's local timezone and local time.
- `GET /` redirects to `/time`.
- The port defaults to 3000. Set the `PORT` environment variable to change it.

